       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Because amlodipine has a long half-life, the effects could last for days.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. Usual doses are:\n- **Starting dose:** 2.5\u20135 mg by mouth once daily\n- **Maintenance dose:** 5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily\n\nPlease confirm what you intended. For example, I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. If you really do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason and I'll add a note to the order. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
